meta {
  name: search ai (page=1 only)
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/search?q=python+csv+parsing&ai=true&page=1
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.snippets: isArray
  res.body.page: eq 1
  res.body.totalPages: isNumber
}

docs {
  AI-resolved search on page=1. The route gates AI resolution behind
  `page === 1`; subsequent pages must reuse the resolved tag/type via
  URL params (no re-resolution). Issue #49.

  Local env runs LLM_PROVIDER=mock so this exercises the deterministic
  mock provider rather than a real LLM. The named mock-script key
  `search-resolves-to-typescript-tag` lands in WU7 — until then this
  request hits the default mock path (which still returns 200; just
  without a guaranteed `aiResolvedFilters` echo).

  Query params:
  - q: search term (required)
  - ai: 'true' enables the AI resolution chain
  - page: must be 1 for AI resolution to fire (gate)
}
